t":0.0,"slope":0.0,"total":0.0},"snow_normal":0.0},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 3 daily record highs, 4 daily record lows","records":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","change":"Fort Pierce's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days warmed over the long run.","rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 76\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>76\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 80\u00b0F, and the record is 87\u00b0F (1986, 1992). The low of <strong>57\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Fort Pierce's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Fort Pierce has set <strong>67 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 81 that chance alone would give, and <strong>87 record highs</strong>, close to the 79 that chance alone would give. The 1990s hold the most record highs of any decade (62). Fort Pierce's all-time high is 101\u00b0F, on June 28, 1950.","t_chg":"Fort Pierce's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days warmed over the long run.","p_chg":"Across 91 complete years: Fort Pierce's average low shows no clear change: \u22120.07\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.17 to +0.03) that includes zero. Fort Pierce's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.17\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.11 to +0.23), about +2.2\u00b0F since 1901. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.89\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.57 to +1.21) and highs show no clear change. The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 6 months fell. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Fort Pierce's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.11 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 53.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1994 (80.24 in); the driest, 1917 (31.73 in). Fort Pierce almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 0.0 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 3 daily record highs, 4 daily record lows"}}